{
  "background_and_question": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "ed6beaa249bdb6b9bd0e3b43b3a53797ff1b8cb468a5d68fdcbd4aea74928da6",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-ed6beaa249bd-0000-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 2,
              "start": 2
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "On April\u202f15,\u202f2013, brothers Dzhokhar and Tamerlan\u202fTsarnaev planted and detonated two pressure\u2011cooker bombs near the finish line of the Boston Marathon, killing three people and injuring hundreds."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Dzhokhar",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "ed6beaa249bdb6b9bd0e3b43b3a53797ff1b8cb468a5d68fdcbd4aea74928da6",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-ed6beaa249bd-0001-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 18,
              "start": 17
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "During sentencing, Dzhokhar sought to introduce evidence that his brother Tamerlan had participated in the 2011 Waltham murders as a mitigating factor, arguing that Tamerlan was the mastermind of the bombing."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Government",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "ed6beaa249bdb6b9bd0e3b43b3a53797ff1b8cb468a5d68fdcbd4aea74928da6",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-ed6beaa249bd-0001-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 12,
              "start": 12
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Government, the legal question before the Supreme Court was whether the district court erred in excluding the Waltham\u2011murder evidence under the Federal Death Penalty Act\u2019s standards for admissibility of mitigating evidence."
      }
    ],
    "heading": "Background and Legal Question",
    "status": "complete",
    "summary": null,
    "summary_citations": []
  },
  "case_id": "2021-20-443",
  "decision": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "ed6beaa249bdb6b9bd0e3b43b3a53797ff1b8cb468a5d68fdcbd4aea74928da6",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-ed6beaa249bd-0001-0006"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 18,
              "start": 18
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The Court held that the Waltham\u2011murder evidence was inadmissible at sentencing."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "ed6beaa249bdb6b9bd0e3b43b3a53797ff1b8cb468a5d68fdcbd4aea74928da6",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-ed6beaa249bd-0001-0006"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 18,
              "start": 18
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The majority held that the Waltham\u2011murder evidence was without probative value and would confuse the jury, and therefore it was properly excluded."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "ed6beaa249bdb6b9bd0e3b43b3a53797ff1b8cb468a5d68fdcbd4aea74928da6",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-ed6beaa249bd-0001-0006"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 18,
              "start": 18
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The Court affirmed the district court\u2019s exclusion of the evidence."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "ed6beaa249bdb6b9bd0e3b43b3a53797ff1b8cb468a5d68fdcbd4aea74928da6",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-ed6beaa249bd-0002-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 24,
              "start": 24
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Barrett, in a concurring opinion, agreed that the evidence would be complex, confusing, and offered little insight into Tamerlan\u2019s role."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "ed6beaa249bdb6b9bd0e3b43b3a53797ff1b8cb468a5d68fdcbd4aea74928da6",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-ed6beaa249bd-0002-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 27,
              "start": 27
            }
          },
          {
            "document_hash": "ed6beaa249bdb6b9bd0e3b43b3a53797ff1b8cb468a5d68fdcbd4aea74928da6",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-ed6beaa249bd-0003-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 32,
              "start": 32
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Breyer dissented, arguing that the evidence met the relevance threshold and that the Court\u2019s supervisory authority over appellate procedural rules lacks a clear constitutional foundation."
      }
    ],
